for one final transformation.

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:34.880
Woo, all right.
(chicken sizzling)

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:38.030
I'm coming off screen with
this coming out of the oven.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:38.980
Oh heck yeah.

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:41.950
Chicken Parm, looking really good.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:44.850
Cheese is all bubbly, skin is crispy.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:46.170
You can still see the basil.

00:11:46.170 --> 00:11:48.700
I think this will be a great plate

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:50.470
for the chicken Parm.

00:11:50.470 --> 00:11:51.933
Hey, pasta goes on first.

00:11:52.996 --> 00:11:54.550
Oh my god, serve that at a restaurant,

00:11:54.550 --> 00:11:56.060
it's like $200.

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:57.460
Yeah, Carbone, where you at?

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.400
Don't actually, I don't, nobody tag them.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:02.060
I want to go to that restaurant,

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:02.990
so I haven't had it before,

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:04.630
so I don't want them to get mad at me.

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:05.463
That's like what?

00:12:05.463 --> 00:12:07.480
Normal serving size for Americans.

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:10.400
This has been the most useful
tool we've had on this show,

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:12.610
and it was designed as
just like a cookie tray.

00:12:12.610 --> 00:12:16.550
But now it has become a scooper,
a chopper, a bench scraper,

00:12:16.550 --> 00:12:17.500
jack of all trades.

00:12:18.636 --> 00:12:19.469
It's great cheese.

00:12:19.469 --> 00:12:21.820
So might as well just
use this cheese on it.

00:12:21.820 --> 00:12:22.653
Is this is what people feel like

00:12:22.653 --> 00:12:24.170
when they go to the strip club,

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.190
and they just throw money.

00:12:25.190 --> 00:12:26.117
I haven't been to one,

00:12:26.117 --> 00:12:28.487
but I would like to try, just
for the experience of it.

00:12:28.487 --> 00:12:31.640
I'm making it rain on the pasta.

00:12:31.640 --> 00:12:33.110
Hi, Mom. (laughs)

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.540
All right, a little bit of basil.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:37.470
Cheese is the only thing
I would probably let rain

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.610
or make rain.

00:12:38.610 --> 00:12:40.630
All right, we're half done.

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:43.453
Heck yeah, right on top you go, big dude.

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.370
Woo, final touch, the sauce.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.740
I think it's a smart move
to put the sauce on top,

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:51.750
not underneath, so that it's not as soggy.

00:12:51.750 --> 00:12:53.170
That's chicken Parm.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:54.340
Make it rain.

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:57.053
Some final touches, there you have it.

00:12:57.053 --> 00:12:59.440
This is very heavy. (laughs)

00:12:59.440 --> 00:13:01.970
This is a quite large chicken Parm.

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:03.740
I think it's time to eat.

00:13:03.740 --> 00:13:06.090
Oh, I need to send a
video to Andrew though.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.150
I want him to see.

00:13:07.150 --> 00:13:09.010
- Alvin, let's take a
look at what you did.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:10.777
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh,
oh, oh, ooh, ooh, ooh.

00:13:12.124 --> 00:13:13.400
Ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh, ooh.

00:13:13.400 --> 00:13:14.650
I think it's big.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.140
I think you made it big.

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:17.470
Alvin, you did me proud.

00:13:17.470 --> 00:13:18.930
You did me so proud.

00:13:18.930 --> 00:13:20.610
It looks unbelievable.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.443
It's huge.

00:13:21.443 --> 00:13:23.930
I love how you said that
both the sauce on top

00:13:23.930 --> 00:13:26.610
and the basil underneath
the cheese were my tips.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.740
Both of those are from
other places, (laughs)

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.680
Carmela Soprano or America's Test Kitchen,

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:31.870
two things that have never been said

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:33.130
in the same sentence before.

00:13:33.130 --> 00:13:34.730
But the pasta looks amazing.

00:13:34.730 --> 00:13:37.950
The chicken Parmesan looks
huge, so mission accomplished.

00:13:37.950 --> 00:13:39.570
The name of the show is "Making It Large,"

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:42.367
(beep) "Making It Giant," (beep)

00:13:42.367 --> 00:13:43.990
"Making It Big." (laughs)

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:46.230
Man, I really wish I could've
been there to eat that.

00:13:46.230 --> 00:13:47.260
It looks incredible.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.170
You did great.

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:50.880
And now all you have to do
is just make it for me again

00:13:50.880 --> 00:13:52.290
when you come over next, okay?

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:54.190
'Cause I'll be hungry, I'll save room.

00:13:55.070 --> 00:13:56.610
Bye, Alvin.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:57.443
- Time to eat.

00:13:57.443 --> 00:14:00.700
I'll just get myself a
little serving of pasta here.

00:14:00.700 --> 00:14:02.803
You can make a normal portion,

00:14:02.803 --> 00:14:05.440
Just like a slice of pizza, oh, heck yeah.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.273
Yeah, look at that.

00:14:06.273 --> 00:14:07.380
Let's go in.

00:14:07.380 --> 00:14:08.640
Cheers.

00:14:08.640 --> 00:14:09.473
For some reason,

00:14:09.473 --> 00:14:11.310
I don't doubt that this
one is gonna taste good,

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:12.547
but we'll see.

00:14:17.092 --> 00:14:21.080
Mm, I was right.

00:14:21.080 --> 00:14:22.310
This does taste good.

00:14:22.310 --> 00:14:24.390
Chicken is nice, pasta is nice.

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:25.600
Everything is nice,

00:14:25.600 --> 00:14:27.600
you know, just a normal meal in America.

00:14:29.557 --> 00:14:30.700
This is pretty good.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:31.850
I wanna finish chewing.

00:14:32.710 --> 00:14:34.270
Well, there we go.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:37.120
I am gonna eat that for quite a long time,

00:14:37.120 --> 00:14:38.390
because it is quite delicious.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.660
I also have a lot of
crew, a lot of friends

00:14:40.660 --> 00:14:41.620
that I could feed that with,

00:14:41.620 --> 00:14:45.030
so I'm not concerned about
taking care of that chicken Parm.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.030
And maybe, I'll give some
to Andrew, who knows?

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.360
But that was it, this is
the end of the season.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:50.410
Thank you, guys, for watching.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:53.690
Again, to watch me go through
a bunch of hoops and hurdles

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:55.800
to try and make a lot of giant versions

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:58.500
of some of the food
that we all like to eat.

00:14:58.500 --> 00:14:59.410
It's been a wild ride.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.680
Huge shout out to the
crew, the culinary team,

00:15:01.680 --> 00:15:03.050
the art team for making things

00:15:03.050 --> 00:15:05.050
like a giant Kit Kat wrapper,

00:15:05.050 --> 00:15:07.550
for the editing team that
is editing this episode

00:15:07.550 --> 00:15:09.310
that you are watching right now.

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:10.310
But that's it for me.

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:11.550
Thank you, guys, for watching

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.376
and I'll see you later.

00:15:13.376 --> 00:15:15.108
Peace.

00:15:15.108 --> 00:15:18.441
(cheerful brass music)

